# ordin-files: files, folders and saved versions
error-file-agent-refused = That file is outside the folder this work can use, so ordin left it alone.
error-file-bin-unavailable = The bin on this computer isn't available. Try again, or move the file yourself.
error-file-changed-meanwhile = That file changed while you were working. Open it again to see the latest version.
error-file-copy-not-found = That shared copy couldn't be found.
error-file-copy-transition-invalid = That shared copy can't be changed in that way right now.
error-file-datastore-unavailable = ordin couldn't reach its record of your files. Try again in a moment.
error-file-doc-kind-unsupported = That kind of file has no text the agent can read.
error-file-doc-no-text = That document has no text that can be read, perhaps because its pages are scanned images. Save a text copy for the agent.
error-file-doc-unreadable = That document couldn't be read. It may be damaged or protected. Save a text copy for the agent.
error-file-folder-unreadable = You don't have permission to read that folder. Choose another folder.
error-file-grant-handoff-failed = ordin couldn't give the agent access to that folder. Try again.
error-file-incoming-refused = That file didn't pass ordin's safety check, so it wasn't added.
error-file-move-target-exists = Another file is already in that place. Choose a different place.
error-file-not-found = That file couldn't be found.
error-file-not-granted = This agent hasn't been given access to that place.
error-file-path-escapes-place = That file location leads outside its folder, so it can't be used.
error-file-place-exists = That folder has already been added.
error-file-place-not-found = That folder couldn't be found in this workspace.
error-file-protected-location = That folder is protected by your computer and can't be added. Choose another folder.
error-file-query-invalid = Search for between 1 and 200 characters. Folders can't be imported as files.
error-file-restore-target-exists = A file is already where this one would go back to. Move or rename it first.
error-file-too-large = That file is too large. ordin handles files up to 64 MB.
error-file-version-copy-missing = The saved copy of that version is missing from this computer.
error-file-version-not-found = That version of the file couldn't be found.
error-file-watch-failed = ordin couldn't start watching that folder for changes. Try adding it again.
error-file-write-failed = ordin couldn't save that file. Check there is enough disk space and try again.
error-fver-latest-prune = The newest version of a file is always kept, so it can't be cleared.
error-fver-path-invalid = That file location isn't valid. Use a location inside the folder that isn't too long.
error-fver-version-gap = ordin couldn't save the next version of that file. Try again.
error-place-name-invalid = Give the folder a name that isn't empty or too long, and has no unusual characters.
error-place-path-invalid = Choose the folder's full location on this computer, and keep it reasonably short.
error-pub-audience-invalid = Describe who the copy is for in between 1 and 500 characters.
error-pub-branch-unexpected = Only a file kept with code can be kept up to date this way.
error-pub-failure-reason-mismatch = A reason for failure goes only with a failed share, and must be 500 characters or fewer.
error-pub-format-destination-mismatch = A page address can only go with a copy shared as a Confluence page.
error-pub-format-maker-mismatch = The exact original file can only be attached to Confluence as it is, without converting it.
error-wf-bundle-path = That location is reserved for ordin and can't be used in a work folder.
error-wf-invalid-namespace = That work folder name isn't valid. Use a simpler name.
error-wf-invalid-path = That location in the work folder isn't valid. Choose another.
error-wf-not-found = That file isn't in the work folder.
error-wf-store-unavailable = The work folder isn't available right now. Try again in a moment.
error-wf-too-large = That file is too large for the work folder. The limit is 10 MB.
